title: call them 'hides from all subscriptions' and 'hides locally'
pid: 80452da9-7ddc-434e-8594-d587d48d7754
body: |2-
  These are more self-explanatory.

  'hides from all subscriptions' does that for, specifically,
  all of the subscriber's owner's subscriptions.

  I am currently only aware of link sources
  as a reason to hide locally (from a link target).

  There could be an 'integrated' folder for each subscription,
  like the 'hides' folder.
  Unfolded, it would show all user-owned containerward paths
  from the subscribee's integrated content.
